---
import ArrowDownIcon from "@/components/icons/ArrowDownIcon";
import FaqItem from "@/components/watch/FaqItem";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import watchCharging from "@/assets/images/charging.svg";
import watchCharged from "@/assets/images/charged.svg";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
---

<Layout>
  <div
    class="bg-content px-5 pb-8 pt-[80px] md:px-8 md:pb-24 md:pt-[108px] xl:px-12"
  >
    <div class="dbs-container relative text-white">
      <div
        class="mt-5 flex flex-col md:mt-20 lg:flex-row lg:items-end lg:justify-between"
      >
        <h1
          class="mr-8 text-4xl font-extralight uppercase sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl xl:text-8xl"
        >
          You may have some questions...
        </h1>
        <div
          class="relative mt-8 max-w-lg pr-12 text-right text-xl font-extralight sm:ml-auto md:text-2xl lg:ml-0 lg:mt-0"
        >
          <p>
            We tried to answer some of those questions that may pop in your
            curious head. For anything else, you can always shoot us an email.
          </p>
          <button class="scroll-trigger absolute bottom-0.5 right-0">
            <ArrowDownIcon className="w-10 h-10" />
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="content bg-white px-5 py-10 md:px-8 md:py-16 xl:px-12 xl:py-24">
    <div
      id="general"
      class="dbs-container relative flex flex-col border-y border-black md:flex-row"
    >
      <div class="sticky top-0 z-10 w-full self-start md:w-fit">
        <h2
          class="w-full space-y-3 border-b border-black/30 bg-white py-6 text-black md:w-48 md:border-b-0 md:py-10 md:text-2xl lg:w-64 xl:w-80"
        >
          <span class="mr-3">1.</span> General
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="basis-full">
        <FaqItem title="Is it water resistant?" showBottomBorder client:idle>
          Yes kind of, you can shower but don’t swim with it.
          <br />
           We got an IP65 rating, to be precise!
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem
          title="How does it handle high and low temperatures?"
          showBottomBorder
          client:idle
        >
          Pretty well to our surprise. We tested our samples at high temperature
          of 85°C and a low of -20°C for 24 hours. We also checked if the watch
          functions under high humidity (85% Relative Humidity to be precise)
          and also tested for 24 hours under thermal shock.
        </FaqItem>
        <!-- TODO: -->
        <FaqItem title="How often do I have to charge the watch?" client:idle>
          On full charge, if clicked for 25 times per day, you might need to
          charge the watch after few weeks (or even a month), it depends heavily
          on your usage.
          <br />
           We made our own automatic robot testing jig to put the theory to
          test. Watch it here.
        </FaqItem>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      id="maintenance"
      class="dbs-container relative flex flex-col border-b border-black md:flex-row md:border-y"
    >
      <div class="sticky top-0 z-10 w-full self-start md:w-fit">
        <h2
          class="w-full space-y-3 border-b border-black/30 bg-white py-6 text-black md:w-48 md:border-b-0 md:py-10 md:text-2xl lg:w-64 xl:w-80"
        >
          <span class="mr-3">1.</span> Maintenance
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="basis-full">
        <!-- TODO: -->
        <FaqItem
          title="How do I reset time (and date)?"
          showBottomBorder
          client:idle
        >
          Yes kind of, you can shower but don’t swim with it.
          <br />
           We got an IP65 rating, to be precise!
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem
          title="How can I change the duration for which the watch displays time on button press?"
          showBottomBorder
          client:idle
        >
          So, we call it the “stay awake” duration and by default it is set to 5
          sec. You can change it by following the previous step of “How do I
          reset time (and Date)?” There, you will see a section, that says,
          “Select Stay awake duration”. But be mindful that a longer stay awake
          duration will lead to faster battery drainage.
        </FaqItem>
        <!-- TODO: -->
        <FaqItem title="How often do I have to charge the watch?" client:idle>
          It’s just like how you charge your other USB devices. Use the provided
          micro USB cable to plug one end of it to the watch and the other to
          any standard 5V DC USB power source (e.g. commonly found phone
          charger). The Yellow light indicated “charging” while the Green means
          “fully charged”.

          <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-6 md:mt-16 md:flex-row">
            <Image src={watchCharging} alt="" />
            <Image src={watchCharged} alt="" />
          </div>
        </FaqItem>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      id="accessories"
      class="dbs-container relative flex flex-col border-b border-black md:flex-row md:border-y"
    >
      <div class="sticky top-0 z-10 w-full self-start md:w-fit">
        <h2
          class="w-full space-y-3 border-b border-black/30 bg-white py-6 text-black md:w-48 md:border-b-0 md:py-10 md:text-2xl lg:w-64 xl:w-80"
        >
          <span class="mr-3">1.</span> Accessories
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="basis-full">
        <FaqItem title="Can I change the belts?" client:idle>
          At the moment the watch ships with the custom belt that we have
          designed and manufactured. In the short term we do not have any plans
          to create a new belt design. But if you would be interested and have
          any suggestions, we are open to the idea. We suggest that you kindly
          drop us a line to share your interests and ideas.
          <br />
          <br />
           Also, since it is so simple to remove the belt, you can experiment
          yourself as well. Currently we are talking to a friend and are
          planning to design an Albert Chain/Necklace for it. We will keep you
          posted about it’s status.
        </FaqItem>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  @media (min-width: 1920px) {
    .dbs-container {
      @apply px-5;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  const button = document.querySelector(".scroll-trigger");
  if (button) {
    button.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const content = document.querySelector(".content");
      if (content) {
        content.scrollIntoView({
          behavior: "smooth",
          block: "start",
          inline: "nearest",
        });
      }
    });
  }
</script>
